eep the degree from printing separately when it has already taken into account in the text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute of the kind element. The degree-value and degree-type text attributes specify how the value and type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the degree should be displayed.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLDegree","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/init(value:alter:kind:printsObject:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"init(value:alter:kind:printsObject:)","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/init(value:alter:kind:printsobject:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV5ValueV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"alter"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV5AlterV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Alter"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV4KindV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Kind"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"printsObject"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/init(value:alter:kind:printsObject:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLDegree"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Value-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"text":"The content of the degree-value type is a number indicating the degree of the chord (1 for the root, 3 for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"third, etc). The text attribute specifies how the value of the degree should be displayed. The symbol","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute indicates that a symbol should be used in specifying the degree. If the symbol attribute is present,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the value of the text attribute follows the symbol.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLDegree.Value","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Value"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Value"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/value-swift.struct","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Value-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Alter-swift.struct":{"title":"MXLDegree.Alter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Alter"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/alter-swift.struct","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct","abstract":[{"text":"The degree-alter type represents the chromatic alteration for the current degree. If the degree-type value is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alter or subtract, the degree-alter value is relative to the degree already in the chord based on its kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element. If the degree-type value is add, the degree-alter is relative to a dominant chord (major and perfect","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"intervals except for a minor seventh). The plus-minus attribute is used to indicate if plus and minus symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"should be used instead of sharp and flat symbols to display the degree alteration. It is no if not specified.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Alter"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Kind-swift.struct":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The degree-type type indicates if this degree is an addition, alteration, or subtraction relative to the kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the current chord. The value of the degree-type element affects the interpretation of the value of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degree-alter element. The text attribute specifies how the type of the degree should be displayed.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLDegree.Kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Kind-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/kind-swift.struct","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Kind"}],"role":"symbol"}}}